# React Compiler Hardening Guidelines

Use these patterns to keep components and hooks compiler-friendly and HMR-stable.

## Core directives

- Keep hook order constant in every render. Avoid any conditional hook calls.

## Patterns to use

- Constant dependency vectors: ensure `useMemo`/`useCallback` dependencies have a fixed length. Hoist constants.
- Use refs to stabilize changing inputs when necessary (e.g., large Sets/Maps) instead of expanding dep arrays.
- Compute derived data in a single `useMemo` with stable deps; avoid multiple interdependent memos.
- Avoid mutating props or hook arguments. Create a local copy or use a setter callback.
  - Example fix implemented in [`packages/ui/src/hooks/use-save-panel-state.ts`](mdc:packages/ui/src/hooks/use-save-panel-state.ts) and its usage in [`packages/ui/src/hooks/use-panel-persistence.ts`](mdc:packages/ui/src/hooks/use-panel-persistence.ts).

## Opt-out policy (dev only)

- If a file causes hook-order/queue errors under HMR, immediately add `'use no memo'` and document in [`plan.md`](mdc:plan.md) with a short rationale and repro.
- Keep prod full-compile enabled while using targeted dev-time opt-outs.

